NEARS-2253 AC2 — Store Panel / VendorApp order-details, no-change baseline.

AC2's premise is FALSE as written and was not chased. It describes a flow reading
delivery-man name/rating/LOCATION. No such flow exists. Measured, not assumed:

STORE PANEL — structurally unreachable from this fix.
  App\Http\Controllers\Vendor\OrderController@details (:212-234) builds its OWN Eloquent
  query, eager-loading delivery_man as delivery_men.* plus an orders_count subselect, and
  passes the raw Order MODEL to view('vendor-views.order.order-view').
  grep -c 'order_data_formatting' app/Http/Controllers/Vendor/OrderController.php = 0
  The projection lives INSIDE order_data_formatting, so it cannot reach this page at all.
  The DM card (vendor-views/order/order-view.blade.php:783-810) prints image_full_url,
  f_name+l_name, orders_count, phone, email. No lat/lng/location anywhere in the card.

  Rendered live against order 163 on the FIX build (read-only):
    delivery_man present : yes
    name                 : D D
    orders_delivered     : 1
    phone rendered       : non-empty
    email rendered       : non-empty
    image_full_url       : non-empty
  Every expression the card prints still resolves. Phone and email still render to the
  store owner here — server-side off the Order model — which is why removing them from the
  API costs no live consumer anything.

VENDORAPP — parses the node, renders none of it, cannot crash on the narrower payload.
  order_model.dart:200 DOES call DeliveryMan.fromJson(json['delivery_man']) on this response.
  Its DeliveryMan (order_model.dart:295-328) declares every field nullable (int? / String?)
  and fromJson uses plain map lookups with NO force-unwrap, so the keys the projection removes
  (phone, email, zone_id, active, application_status) simply arrive null.
  The only render block, order_details_screen.dart:842-899 — tel: launcher included — is
  commented out in its entirety. No other live consumer of order.deliveryMan exists in lib/.
  VendorApp parses no lat/lng: the model has no such fields.

The phpunit AC2 intact-guard (assertDeliveryManNodeIntact) additionally pins that all ten
allow-listed keys are still present and that delivery_man is an OBJECT, not a list.
